docs/architecture-audit.md
docs/Rapport Fusion Account.txt
docs/règles_filtre.txt
docs/regex-filter-plan.md
docs/responsive-consistency-audit.md
docs/i18n.md
docs/superpowers/

# Security programme working artifacts: the ASVS 5.0 map and its generators, the #184 pentest
# harnesses, and the throwaway credentials those harnesses were run with. Local only, one
# machine, no backup, the same arrangement as docs/superpowers/ above.
#
# Tracked as an ignore rule rather than left as a local working-tree edit, and the reason is
# worth keeping: this directory holds live private keys (eb_key.pem, eb_stub_key.pem), captured
# cookie jars and a TOTP secret. An unignored `git add -A` publishes them to a public
# repository. The rule was twice lost to a `git reset --hard` that discarded the working-tree
# edit carrying it, in one afternoon, which is exactly as often as it takes.
scripts/security/

# Local-only agent instructions (public shared file is AGENTS.md)
/CLAUDE.md
# Per-machine Claude Code permissions (shared config is .claude/settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Playwright MCP browser session artifacts (page snapshots, downloads)
.playwright-mcp/

# Throwaway viewport-audit screenshots. Same rule as .playwright-mcp/ above: a harness that
# writes into the repo will be swept in by `git add -A` on the next commit, and 312K of them
# already merged once that way (#112).
e2e/.audit390/

# Serena MCP local project state. project.yml is meant to be versioned with the project
# (per Serena's own docs); cache, memories and project.local.yml are local-only.
.serena/
# Serena's own project config was tracked until 0.13.0, on the theory that a shared
# `project_name` was worth one file. It is not: the MCP server REWRITES it on session start,
# stripping its comment block, so every session that touched this repository produced a
# modified working tree and a prettier warning nobody introduced. Local tool configuration
# that regenerates itself belongs to the machine, not to the clone. A fresh clone simply
# re-onboards, which costs one prompt and nothing else.

# Golden master harness and its captures. Same rule as e2e/.audit390 above: a harness that writes
# into the repo gets swept in by `git add -A`, and a capture is hundreds of kilobytes of generated
# JSON with no forward readership. It is a CONVENIENCE on this list, not a control: nothing here
# protects anything, so losing the rule costs a noisy diff rather than a secret. If the config is
# ever judged worth versioning, `git add -f vitest.golden.config.ts` and move that line out.
/golden-master/
/vitest.golden.config.ts

# Scratch for scripts/test-env.sh: generated Compose overlay and synthetic fixtures.
/.test-env/
